<section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="tour-detail-layout">
  <div class="tour-detail-main reveal">
    <h2>Tour Overview</h2>
    <p>Two of the world's greatest travel experiences in one journey. Begin on the ancient Silk Road through Xi'an, Dunhuang, and Kashgar — then board the world's highest railway to Tibet. Walk through the Potala Palace, stand before Everest Base Camp, and witness monks debating at Sera Monastery. From the golden deserts of the Taklamakan to the snowy peaks of the Himalayas — this is the adventure of a lifetime.</p>

    <div class="highlight-box"><h3>Trip Highlights</h3><ul>
      <li>Terracotta Warriors in Xi'an</li><li>Mogao Caves in Dunhuang</li>
      <li>Kashgar Sunday Bazaar</li>
      <li>Ride the Qinghai-Tibet Railway — world's highest</li>
      <li>Potala Palace — the heart of Tibet</li>
      <li>Jokhang Temple & Barkhor Circuit</li>
      <li>Monk debate at Sera Monastery</li>
      <li>Yamdrok Lake — turquoise jewel of Tibet</li>
    </ul></div>

    <h2>Day-by-Day Itinerary</h2>
    <ul class="itinerary">
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>1</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Arrive in Xi'an</h4><p>Airport pickup, hotel check-in. Evening stroll through the Muslim Quarter and Bell Tower square. Welcome dinner featuring Xi'an's famous dumpling banquet.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Xi'an 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>2</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Xi'an — Terracotta Warriors</h4><p>Full morning at the Terracotta Warriors — 8,000 life-sized soldiers guarding China's first emperor. Afternoon bike ride on the ancient City Wall (14 km loop). Visit Big Wild Goose Pagoda.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Xi'an 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>3</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Xi'an &#8594; Dunhuang (Flight)</h4><p>Morning flight to Dunhuang. Afternoon at the Dunhuang Museum for Silk Road context. Evening camel ride at Singing Sand Dunes to watch the sunset.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Dunhuang 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>4</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Dunhuang — Mogao Caves</h4><p>Full morning at the Mogao Caves — 1,000 years of Buddhist art in 492 grottoes. Afternoon at Crescent Moon Spring and sand boarding on the dunes.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Dunhuang 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>5</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Dunhuang &#8594; Turpan (High-speed train)</h4><p>Morning train to Turpan (4 hrs). Afternoon visit to Jiaohe Ancient City — one of the world's best-preserved earthen cities. Grape Valley tasting.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Turpan 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>6</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Turpan — Flaming Mountains & Karez</h4><p>Morning at the Flaming Mountains and Bezeklik Thousand Buddha Caves. Tour the ancient Karez irrigation tunnels. Visit Emin Minaret.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Turpan 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>7</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Turpan &#8594; Urumqi &#9992; Kashgar</h4><p>Drive to Urumqi, visit the Xinjiang Museum to see the Tarim mummies. Afternoon flight to Kashgar. Evening tea at a 100-year-old teahouse.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Kashgar 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>8</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kashgar — Sunday Market & Karakoram</h4><p>Experience the legendary Sunday Bazaar. Drive the Karakoram Highway to Karakul Lake for jaw-dropping views of Muztagh Ata (7,546m).</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Kashgar 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>9</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kashgar &#9992; Xining — Qinghai-Tibet Railway</h4><p>Morning flight to Xining. Free afternoon to acclimatize. Evening: board the legendary Qinghai-Tibet Railway — the world's highest train journey begins!</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#128646; Overnight Train</span><span>&#127860; B</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>10</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>On the Roof of the World — Arrive Lhasa</h4><p>Wake up crossing the Tibetan Plateau at 5,000m. Views of snow-capped peaks, yaks, and turquoise lakes. Arrive in Lhasa afternoon. Rest and acclimatize.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Lhasa 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>11</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Lhasa — Potala Palace & Jokhang Temple</h4><p>The big day. Morning at the Potala Palace — 1,000 rooms, 13 stories, the spiritual heart of Tibet. Afternoon at Jokhang Temple, Tibet's holiest shrine. Join pilgrims on the Barkhor kora.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Lhasa 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>12</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Lhasa — Sera & Drepung Monasteries</h4><p>Morning at Drepung Monastery — once the world's largest monastery housing 10,000 monks. Afternoon at Sera Monastery to witness the famous monk debates — a centuries-old tradition.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Lhasa 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>13</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Lhasa &#8594; Yamdrok Lake &#8594; Gyantse</h4><p>Drive over the Kamba La Pass (4,794m) for the first breathtaking view of Yamdrok Lake — one of Tibet's three holy lakes. Continue to Gyantse, visit Pelkor Chode Monastery.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Gyantse 3&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>14</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Gyantse &#8594; Shigatse — Tashilhunpo Monastery</h4><p>Drive to Shigatse, Tibet's second city. Visit Tashilhunpo Monastery, seat of the Panchen Lama. The giant Maitreya Buddha statue (26m) is awe-inspiring.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Shigatse 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>15</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Depart Lhasa</h4><p>Drive back to Lhasa Airport along the Yarlung Tsangpo River. Farewell to the roof of the world. &#20877;&#35265;!</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127860; B</span></div></div></li>
    </ul>

